# Line endings: the repo stores LF, so check LF out everywhere.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true hands Windows a CRLF working tree while git
# keeps LF blobs. Nothing is wrong in the repo, but `deno fmt` writes LF, so
# `deno fmt --check` fails on every file it looks at — and running `deno fmt`
# to "fix" it produces no git diff at all, which is thoroughly confusing. It
# also leaves files permanently stat-dirty (the CRLF and LF forms differ in
# size, so git re-flags them as modified until the content is re-read).
#
# eol=lf overrides core.autocrlf, so this holds regardless of a contributor's
# local git config.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never apply line-ending conversion. `text=auto` already
# detects these by content, but spelling them out keeps the heuristic well
# away from the sprite atlases, the bitmap font and any recordings.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.webm binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
